💡 Final Answer: A mean reversion strategy is a trading approach that capitalizes on the tendency of financial asset prices to revert to their historical mean or average price over time. It identifies trading opportunities in markets that have moved excessively away from their historical averages. Its profitability depends on its design, the markets used, and how strictly it is executed.
